    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0431" n="419" xml:id="pg419"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/7–344: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ford</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-03T09:00:00+03:25">July 3, 1944—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:57 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>474. Millspaugh informs me Prime Minister yesterday expressed to Majlis his
                    confidence United States Mission and supported Millspaugh proposal that question
                    of economic powers be allowed to rest 3 or 4 months to give time for results of
                    mission’s operations to become visible. Majority of Majlis was favorable and
                    Millspaugh regards immediate crisis as past and that he has won victory.</p>
                <p>In view of this classification [<hi rendition="#italic">clarification?</hi>] of
                    status of road transport directors am authorizing resumption of Lend Lease
                        deliveries.<anchor n="18" xml:id="d435-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d435-f1" n="18" xml:id="d435-f1-content">
                <p>The Chargé had temporarily held in abeyance the delivery of unpaid for Lend-Lease
                    goods then in Iran awaiting delivery to the Iranian Government; he had taken
                    this action on his own initiative in connection with another matter involving
                    technical considerations and unrelated to policy matters.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
